# --- Byte-governed by other gates ---
# `check-design-system.mjs` compares each registry entry's @case markup byte-for-byte
# against DEMO_SNIPPETS in demo-host.component.ts, and `check-design-guides.mjs` reads
# each article's tab bodies to decide which selectors and files a guide claims. Both
# parse this tree as text, so reformatting it makes them report drift that is not there
# — a formatter and a byte-comparison gate cannot both own the same file.
src/app/dev/

# --- Prose. Prettier formats code here, not documents. ---
# Markdown in this repo is written to be read, and three gates govern it by content:
# check-design-guides.mjs holds each agent doc to a byte budget, check-design-system.mjs
# compares guide markup byte-for-byte against DEMO_SNIPPETS, and check-doc-drift.mjs
# pins each translated mirror to a hash of its source. Prettier's markdown printer
# reflows all three out of true (it also rewrites *emphasis* as _emphasis_), so running
# it over prose costs six guides their budget and every mirror its marker, and buys
# nothing a reader would notice. One template is worse still: it never converges —
# `--write` then `--check` still reports packs/editor/assets/templates/style-review.vorlage.md.
*.md
*.MD

